  "title": "pool.claude_split(cfg, card) moves the claude:sonnet/claude:opus line by evidence; eligible_executors routes Claude rows by it; status() tolerates a missing [codex] table",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, plan label B1. Contract (plan.md): pool.claude_split(cfg, card) -> int; config\n[routing] sonnet_max_complexity, split_min, split_max, split_min_samples.\n\nFacts (main 355583c):\n- orchestrator/pool.py:577-597 eligible_executors() filters rows by enabled/role/cooling, then by the row band\n  `ex.complexity_min <= complexity <= ex.complexity_max` (584), parallelism, daily budget, and Claude account\n  headroom (591-595). pick_executor() (599-620) ranks the eligible rows; codex_available() (651-659) also calls\n  eligible_executors().\n- Shipped rows (.orchestrator/pool.toml ~252-274): claude:sonnet complexity 1-5, claude:opus 6-10. The line is\n  static; nothing reads evidence for it. There is no top-level [routing] table yet ([planner.routing] and\n  [jev.routing] are unrelated sub-tables).\n- The evidence source is the scorecard card: orchestrator/scorecard.py:179 build(root, by=\"executor\") returns\n  {executor_id: {\"merged\", \"failed\", \"by_complexity\": {\"1-3\"|\"4-6\"|\"7-10\": {\"merged\", \"failed\"}}, ...}}; bands\n  come from attribution.band() (orchestrator/attribution.py:118-125).\n- pool.py:680 status() reads self.cfg[\"codex\"][\"on_exhausted\"] and raises KeyError when pool.toml has no [codex]\n  table (a Claude-only config).\n\nChange:\n1. Add module function claude_split(cfg, card) -> int in pool.py:\n   r = cfg.get(\"routing\", {}); base = int(r.get(\"sonnet_max_complexity\", 5)); lo = int(r.get(\"split_min\", 4));\n   hi = int(r.get(\"split_max\", 7)); n_min = int(r.get(\"split_min_samples\", 10));\n   floor = cfg.get(\"models\", {}).get(\"success_floor\", 0.6); clamp base into [lo, hi].\n   rate(eid, c): the row card.get(eid, {}).get(\"by_complexity\", {}).get(attribution.band(c)) -> (merged/n, n), n =\n   merged + failed, (None, 0) when n == 0. Then:\n   - if base + 1 <= hi and sonnet n at base+1 >= n_min and sonnet rate >= floor and (opus n at base+1 < n_min or\n     sonnet rate >= opus rate): return base + 1\n   - elif base - 1 >= lo and sonnet n at base >= n_min and sonnet rate < floor: return base - 1\n   - else return base.\n   Pure: no disk reads; card may be {} or missing keys.\n2. Pool gets a lazily computed split: a method Pool.claude_split() that builds the card once per Pool instance\n   (from .scorecard import build; any exception -> card {}) and caches claude_split(self.cfg, card).\n3. eligible_executors(): only when BOTH claude:sonnet and claude:opus rows exist and are enabled, replace the row\n   band check for those two rows: claude:sonnet is eligible iff complexity_min <= complexity <= split;\n   claude:opus iff split < complexity <= complexity_max. Every other row (codex rows, haiku, a lone Claude row)\n   keeps its row band exactly as today. pick_executor and codex_available inherit this through\n   eligible_executors; do not add a second filter.\n4. status(): read on_exhausted with self.cfg.get(\"codex\", {}).get(\"on_exhausted\", \"hold\").\n5. .orchestrator/pool.toml: add ONLY a new top-level [routing] table with sonnet_max_complexity = 5, split_min = 4,\n   split_max = 7, split_min_samples = 10 and a one-line comment each. Touch nothing else in that file: codex rows\n   stay enabled in the committed file (PR 28 trap; Codex-off is a live-only change).\n\nTests that assert the old behaviour (SPEC RULE; update them to the new contract, do not delete coverage):\n- tests/test_pool.py::test_claude_row_needs_account_headroom (ExecutorIdentity, ~506-521) builds both Claude rows\n  (claude:opus copied from the 1-10 sonnet fixture) and expects claude:opus eligible at complexity 3. Under the\n  split it is not; update the expected lists (or the complexity used) so the test still proves the headroom rule.\n- tests/test_pool.py::test_repo_config_has_claude_rows (~149-162) must still pass unchanged (3 -> sonnet,\n  8 -> opus with the default split).\n- Run tests/test_pool.py, tests/test_executor.py and tests/test_scorecard.py (focused, foreground); they build\n  pools with Claude rows.\n\nOut of scope: B2's daemon/executor changes, scorecard.py, attribution.py.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_claude_split_moves_line_by_evidence: passes: claude_split returns [routing].sonnet_max_complexity (default 5) with no evidence, base+1 when claude:sonnet has >= split_min_samples resolved tasks in the band of base+1 at or above models.success_floor (and not below claude:opus there), base-1 when sonnet is below the floor in its own band, never outside [split_min, split_max]; with both claude rows enabled and split 6, pick_executor('execute', 6) is claude:sonnet and pick_executor('execute', 7) is claude:opus",
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_status_without_codex_table: passes: Pool(cfg without a [codex] table).status() returns a dict (codex.on_exhausted 'hold') instead of raising KeyError",
